        "detail": "Fig. 7 \"Base-emitter voltage as a function of collector current; typical values\", VCE = 2 V, curve (2) Tamb = 25 C Method: Pixel-digitized curve (2): IC=0.105 mA VBE=0.5405 V; 0.217 mA 0.5595; 0.472 mA 0.5811; 1.05 mA 0.6014; 2.23 mA 0.6203; 10.5 mA 0.6595; 22.9 mA 0.6811 V. Log fit over 0.1-23 mA gives 59.5 mV/decade, i.e. N = 1.005, so N=1 is consistent. IS = IC/exp(VBE/Vt) with Vt = kT/q at 298.15 K (25.69 mV) gives 7.0e-14..7.7e-14 per point, mean 7.4e-14 (free-N fit 8.3e-14). Above ~0.1 A the curve bends up (high injection/RB), so those points are excluded. Assumes Tj = Tamb = 25 C. A +/-3 mV read error moves IS about +/-12%. Consistency: read VBE 0.815 V at 0.51 A is below the Table 7 max \"VBE ... VCE = 2 V; IC = 500 mA ... 1 V\". Replaces the 1e-14 assumption (factor ~7).",
